. *==============================================================================
. *** 5. Child penalty in % of counterfactual earnings (bootstrap SEs)
. *==============================================================================
. * For comparability purpouses,  we express earnings loss as a % of what treated mothers would have earned without the birth.
. * Counterfactual earnings of the treated = observed mean - estimated effect, so penalty(t) = sum_s w_s*b_st / sum_s w_s*(ybar_st - b_st), w_s = share of trea
> ted people.
. * The ratio has no analytic SE -> cluster bootstrap over individuals.
. * Index k = event time + 3 (k = 2, i.e. t = -1, is the reference period).
. 
. *** 5a) Stacked data with the same event-time dummies as in 4a
. use "$out/stacked_data.dta", clear

. forvalues s = $s_min/$s_max {
  2.     foreach k in 0 1 3 4 5 6 7 {
  3.         gen d_s`s'_l`k' = subevent == `s' & treatedsubevent == 1 & evtime == `k' - $P
  4.     }
  5. }

. *** 5b) Define a program that runs the full estimation once and returns the results
. * (since bootstrap needs the estimation wrapped in a program so it can rerun it)
. capture program drop child_penalty

. program define child_penalty, rclass
  1.     args id                                   // pid, or the bootstrap id
  2.         * Weights count each treated person once per sub-event
.     quietly reghdfe labearnings d_s*_l*, absorb(`id'#subevent age#subevent)
  3.     tempvar first                             // each treated person once per sub-event
  4.     quietly bysort subevent `id': gen `first' = _n == 1 & treatedsubevent == 1
  5.     quietly count if `first'
  6.     local N = r(N)
  7.     foreach k in 0 1 3 4 5 6 7 {
  8.         local num = 0
  9.         local den = 0
 10.         forvalues s = $s_min/$s_max {
 11.             quietly count if `first' & subevent == `s'
 12.             local w = r(N) / `N'
 13.             quietly summarize labearnings if treatedsubevent == 1 & subevent == `s' & evtime == `k' - $P, meanonly
 14.             local num = `num' + `w' * _b[d_s`s'_l`k']
 15.             local den = `den' + `w' * (r(mean) - _b[d_s`s'_l`k'])
 16.         }
 17.         local b`k'   = `num'
 18.         local pct`k' = 100 * `num' / `den'  // effect in % of counterfactual earnings
 19.     }
 20.     foreach k in 0 1 3 4 5 6 7 {             
 21.         return scalar b`k'   = `b`k''
 22.         return scalar pct`k' = `pct`k''
 23.     }
 24. end

. 
. *** 5c) Cluster bootstrap over individuals
. * I resample people instead of rows since a person appears in several sub-events, so all their rows must be drawn together. idcluster() gives each drawn copy
>  a new id.
. gen bs_pid = pid

. bootstrap b0=r(b0) b1=r(b1) b3=r(b3) b4=r(b4) b5=r(b5) b6=r(b6) b7=r(b7)             ///
>           pct0=r(pct0) pct1=r(pct1) pct3=r(pct3) pct4=r(pct4) pct5=r(pct5)            ///
>           pct6=r(pct6) pct7=r(pct7), reps(500) seed(2026) cluster(pid) idcluster(bs_pid): ///
>           child_penalty bs_pid
